0..64 Comment "// A reflexivity at a point composes with `Path.step` in a type."
65..67 Comment "//"
68..149 Comment "// `Path.here(x)` reads its type off its point\'s binder, whatever type the binder"
150..232 Comment "// writes: `Path[.A = A](x, x)` when `x : A`. A composite whose first operand is a"
233..298 Comment "// reflexivity, or ends in one, takes its type from that reading."
299..301 Comment "//"
302..362 Comment "// Each declaration states such a composite in its own type."
363..365 Comment "//"
366..436 Comment "// - see: #3834 — a reflexivity first in a composite, refused before"
438..513 Comment "/// A reflexivity stands first in the type\'s composite. The left unit holds"
514..590 Comment "/// up to a path, not by computation, so the composite stands on both sides."
591..594 Keyword "def"
595..604 FunctionDef "hereFirst"
